    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • XPENG Reveals G9L at the 2026 Paris Motor Show, Dubbed As the Ultimate \"Large SUV for the AI Era\"\nOMODA 4 Lands in Paris To Showcase Futuristic Styling, Looks Like a Discount Urus\n23 photos\nPhoto: OMODA\nOne of the Chery Group’s latest compact SUVs, the OMODA 4, just made its European motor show debut in Paris this week, ahead of its UK market launch in 2027. This also marks OMODA&JAECOO’s first-ever appearance at the French event.\nThe OMODA 4 was originally unveiled at Auto China 2026, showcasing not only its futuristic styling, but also the carmaker’s proprietary Super Hybrid System (SHS-H). It’s the styling I want to focus on, though, because it’s meant to be the boldest expression yet of the brand’s so-called “Cyber Mecha” design language.\nAs you can see, there are a lot of sharp lines. You certainly can’t accuse the design of being old-fashioned. To me, this crossover also looks a little bit like a discount Lamborghini Urus, which both is and isn’t a bad thing.\nThe carmaker seems to be particularly pleased with the interior, calling it a “technology-led starship cockpit”. It was inspired by gaming and digital environments, while reflecting OMODA’s “BE THE ONE” philosophy. Like the OMODA 5, the 4 is also aimed at a younger, technology-focused buyer, which is why the cabin has somewhat of a sporty design.\nTo all that I say, give me a break! I mean, even the starter button looks like it’s from an Urus , featuring a red button cover. How hard is it to come up with something original? Or at least something generic. If the car is good enough on its own, it shouldn’t need to blatantly steal various design elements from other models.\nPhoto: Omoda Here’s what Gary Lan, CEO of OMODA&JAECOO UK had to say: “Our Paris debut is an important moment for OMODA, and it’s fantastic that OMODA 4 has now made its European motor show debut.”\n“OMODA has always had a strong sense of individuality, and I think this new model really captures that while also representing an important part of the brand’s future. It’s youthful, fashion-conscious and technology-led, bringing a fresh perspective to the crossover market and appealing to customers who want something a little different.”\nIn terms of performance, we can expect the OMODA 4 SHS-H to feature the same drivetrain as the OMODA 5 SHS-H, meaning a hybrid system with 224 horsepower and 295 Nm (217 lb-ft) of torque. This allows the 5 to hit 62 mph (100 kph) in 7.9 seconds, so the smaller 4 could be a tiny bit quicker off the mark.\nThere are currently three models available to UK buyers from OMODA, with the 4 set to join the group come next year. Right now, though, you can only order the OMODA 5, OMODA 7 and the 9. The entry-level 5 is priced from £24,040 in gasoline spec, but you can also get an all-electric E5 for upwards of £33,065. Meanwhile, the flagship OMODA 9 SHS-P is a $44,995 affair.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nOmoda 4 OMODAJAECOO omoda Chery Hybrid 2026 Paris Motor Show Paris Motor Show\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Sergiu Tudose\nSergiu got to experience both American and European car \"scenes\" at an early age (his father drove a Ford Fiesta XR2 supermini in the 80s). After spending over 15 years at local and international auto publications, he's starting to appreciate comfort behind the wheel more than raw power and acceleration. Full profile\nUP NEXT The 2027 Bailey Unicorn Grande Lucena Is a Fancy Home on Wheels in Travel Trailer Disguise",
